+    /**
+     * Registers a parsed type, keyed by name.
+     * <p>
+     * Bug fix: {@code SourceParser.parseStruct} is called for every
+     * {@code STRUCT_DECL}/{@code CLASS_DECL} cursor, including bare forward
+     * declarations ({@code class Foo;}) that have no children at all -- it has
+     * no {@code isDefinition()} check to skip them (no such binding exists on
+     * {@code Cursor} yet). In any codebase where a class is forward-declared
+     * again *after* its full definition is visited in the same translation
+     * unit -- extremely common; CommonLibSSE-NG alone forward-declares
+     * classes like {@code TESForm} in dozens of files -- the forward
+     * declaration produces an empty {@code ParsedStructure} (zero fields)
+     * that used to unconditionally overwrite the real, already-parsed
+     * definition here, silently truncating it to a zero-size stub with no
+     * diagnostic. Confirmed live: parsing CommonLibSSE-NG's TESForm/
+     * TESObject/TESBoundObject/TESObjectREFR chain produced zero clang
+     * errors, yet TESForm ended up as an empty struct in the final archive.
+     * <p>
+     * Fix: when both the existing and incoming entries are
+     * {@link ParsedStructure}s, keep whichever has more fields -- a real
+     * definition always has at least as many fields as any forward
+     * declaration of the same class (which always has zero), so this needs
+     * no new libclang binding and can't misfire the other direction (a
+     * struct never "loses" fields between two full-definition visits of the
+     * same translation unit).
+     */
     public void addParsedType(ParsedType type) {
+        ParsedType existing = this.parsedTypes.get(type.getName());
+        if (existing instanceof ParsedStructure existingStruct
+            && type instanceof ParsedStructure incomingStruct
+            && incomingStruct.getFields().size() < existingStruct.getFields().size()) {
+            LOGGER.debug("Keeping existing definition of '{}' ({} fields) over incoming "
+                + "forward declaration ({} fields)", type.getName(),
+                existingStruct.getFields().size(), incomingStruct.getFields().size());
+            return;
+        }
         this.parsedTypes.put(type.getName(), type);
     }
 
